105
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:30,440
And of those deputies, a lot of those are very big revolutionary names.

106
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:34,780
So the top of the list, number one, their top choice for Paris is Robespierre.

107
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:41,900
And then you've got people like Danton, Desmoulins, Santerre, the butcher, the sans-culottes who'd led the attack on the Tuileries.

108
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:48,640
Marat, for the first time, this firebrand radical journalist, he is going to have a seat in the convention.

109
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:56,740
So there will be a place for the most extreme, the most violent, the most paranoid revolutionary sentiments.

110
00:06:57,020 --> 00:07:00,020
And there's a place, isn't there, for the worst man in the entire history of the French Revolution?

111
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:00,780
Yeah.

112
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:04,920
The erstwhile Duke of Orléans, the cousin of Louis XVI.

113
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,540
Philip Egalité.

114
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,140
I mean, we've talked about this before.

