And that man is a guy called general Charles Francois Dumouriez.

205
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:19,080
So listeners may remember he's this kind of grizzled, ex secret agent, ex seven years war veteran who was foreign minister under the Girondins.

206
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,440
He got France into this mess in the first place.

207
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:24,520
And basically he's in charge of the Eastern front.

208
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:27,760
He really wanted to, he loves fighting Belgians.

209
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:29,140
He loves attacking Belgium.

210
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:29,960
That's his dream.

211
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,720
He wants to liberate Belgium.

212
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:35,180
The convention has basically said, forget about Belgium.

213
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:39,980
Like there's a, there are a load of Prussians advancing on Paris, get to the valley of the Marne and stop them.

214
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:45,260
There's a lot of maneuvering and faffing around in the ever kind.

215
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:47,060
Do you want to, to go into detail about that?

216
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:56,780
I, do you know what I could, I could, but I won't because I don't want to try the patience of our less military minded listeners.

217
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:58,220
Exactly.

218
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,740
How many divisions are there on both sides?

219
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:02,000
Loads.

220
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:11,280
So to cut a very long story short, the two armies end up faffing around and maneuvering, and basically they end up on the wrong side of each other.

221
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:19,100
So the Prussians are nearest Paris and Jumurier is behind them with his back against the Argonne forest.

222
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:24,400
Now the Duke of Brunswick could just ignore Jumurier and could have just dashed on, couldn't he to Paris?

223
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:31,760
He could, but he doesn't want to do that because he, that would mean Jumurier could cut his supply lines, basically cut him off from the German states.

224
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:40,980
And his men are very muddy and it's pouring rain, they're knackered, they're short of food, they're ravaged by illness.

